BT /F2 9.5 Tf 0.2 0.5 0.8 rg 57 686 Td (Q1: Why did you use an ESP32 hardware node when modern smartphones already have accelerometers?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 57 672 Td (ANSWER: Smartphones are mechanically decoupled from the vehicle chassis. When a driver picks up their phone, adjusts navigation, or the phone) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 57 659.5 Td (slides on a passenger seat, it experiences 2.0g - 3.5g surges, causing false harsh-braking and crash triggers in phone-only apps.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 57 647 Td (Furthermore, phone sensors are clamped by the mobile OS to +/-2g or +/-4g, causing them to clip/saturate during real crashes.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 57 634.5 Td (Our ESP32 node is rigidly fixed to the chassis, has zero handheld noise, and is configured to full +/-16g collision range.) Tj ET
