BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 57 592 Td (ANSWER: Potholes generate an abrupt vertical acceleration shockwave on the vehicle suspension while lateral and longitudinal forces remain low.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 57 579.5 Td (Our algorithm checks three conditions simultaneously: \(1\) Vehicle transit speed >= 12 km/h \(to ignore door slams\), \(2\) Absolute vertical Z-axis) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 0.15 0.18 0.22 rg 57 567 Td (force |az| >= 1.90g, and \(3\) Vertical dominance ratio |az| > horizontalG * 1.25. When all 3 pass, it geotags a pothole with a 4-second debounce.) Tj ET
